n Ben had used, that opposite charges attract and her hair was proving it live, right now, in front of them. One of the younger judges laughed out loud and asked her to do it again.\n\nBen won a certificate for Scientific Rigour. Zara won a certificate for Most Engaging Demonstration, and spent the rest of the afternoon being asked by at least a dozen other children to do the hair trick again, which she was, by that point, extremely happy to keep doing.","orderedAnswer":["forgetting the project was due","preparing her project","the judges coming round","receiving her certificate"],"validationTier":"TIER4_ORDERED_LIST"}$json$,
 'Educational Increment 007C completion. Assessment Brain QT-RC-06, primary competency RC-04. Question family: wave1-fam-sequencing. Transfer class: NEAR_TRANSFER. Real evidence basis: direct reading of CSSE-003/005/008/013 (2021/2022/2023 Main Test papers and 2023 marking scheme, Level A, Founder-Accepted), reconciled in Educational Increments 007A/007B/007C. Answer validation: TIER4_ORDERED_LIST.', 2, 'wave2-eng-sciencefair',
